/-!
# The homogeneous ideal of a closed subscheme of Proj

Let `S` carry a nonnegative grading `𝒮` and let `i : Z ⟶ Proj 𝒮` be a closed immersion. A
homogeneous element `a` of degree `n` is an *equation for* `Z` when the global section of
`𝒪(n)` it determines pulls back to zero on `Z`. The ideal generated by all such elements is
the homogeneous ideal of `Z`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealOfClosedSubscheme.idealOfClosedSubscheme`: the ideal of a
  closed subscheme of a projective spectrum.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealOfClosedSubscheme.mem_idealOfClosedSubscheme_iff`: the
  degreewise criterion, that an arbitrary element lies in the ideal exactly when every one of
  its homogeneous components does.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealOfClosedSubscheme.idealOfClosedSubscheme_isHomogeneous`: the
  ideal is homogeneous.

## Implementation notes

The ideal is defined as the span of the homogeneous equations rather than as the kernel of the
canonical graded map `S → ⨁ n, Γ(Proj 𝒮, 𝒪(n))` of Tag 01MP, because that graded ring map is
not available: its construction requires the multiplication on twisted sections, which is Tag
01MP's content and is not formalized. `mem_idealOfClosedSubscheme_iff` identifies the span with
that kernel degreewise, so nothing is lost: the two descriptions agree on every element, not
only on homogeneous ones.

The degreewise criterion is proved by showing that the set of elements all of whose components
pull back to zero is already an ideal. Additivity comes from the additivity of
`degreeSectionHom`, and stability under multiplication is reduced by
`DirectSum.Decomposition.inductionOn` to multiplication by a homogeneous element, where the
relevant component of the product is a single product of components and the naturality of
`degreeZeroToGlobalSections` (Tag 01M7) applies.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BXK](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BXK)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01M7](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01M7)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01MN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01MN)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

